
 Statistics behind Section 5.3 of the paper, as produced by `python -m scripts.fairness_statistics` on the reported runs.

   fairness_stats_cg.csv   one row per (dataset, scenario, split, recommender, algorithm):
                           group sizes, signed difference, 95% bootstrap CI, permutation p,
                           Holm-adjusted p, Cohen's d, detectable difference (mde).
   fairness_stats_pig.csv  same keys: recommender gap and summary gap with CIs,
                           amplification ratio with CI, change of the gap with CI,
                           permutation p and Holm-adjusted p.
